#: ../../site/guides/portfolio-risk.md:59
msgid "Preconditions and statuses:"
msgstr "前置条件与状态："

#: ../../site/guides/portfolio-risk.md:61
msgid ""
"The index must be strictly ascending and duplicate-free; `NaN` observations "
"are dropped first. An empty result set, an unsorted or duplicated index, or "
"an invalid configuration raises `input_error`."
msgstr "索引必须严格升序且无重复；先丢弃 `NaN` 观测。结果为空、索引乱序或重复、配置非法都会抛 `input_error`。"

#: ../../site/guides/portfolio-risk.md:64
msgid ""
"`status` is `ok` when at least two non-`NaN` observations were usable and "
"any GARCH fit converged, `insufficient_data` when fewer than two remained, "
"and `failed` when a GARCH fit did not converge or failed its stationarity "
"checks. A non-converged GARCH fit also fills `note`."
msgstr ""
"当至少有两个可用非 `NaN` 观测且任何 GARCH 拟合都收敛时 `status` 为 `ok`；剩余少于两个时为 "
"`insufficient_data`；GARCH 拟合未收敛或未通过平稳性检查时为 `failed`。未收敛的 GARCH 拟合还会填写 "
"`note`。"

#: ../../site/guides/portfolio-risk.md:68
msgid ""
"`inputs_digest` is a lowercase SHA-256 over the cleaned timestamps and "
"values, so two runs can be compared without comparing floats."
msgstr "`inputs_digest` 是对清洗后时间戳与数值的小写 SHA-256，因此两次运行可以在不比较浮点的情况下对照。"

#: ../../site/guides/portfolio-risk.md:70
msgid ""
"Under the GARCH family, `garch_model::egarch` recurses on the **log** "
"variance, so a negative `omega` is admissible there while the GARCH and GJR "
"`omega` intercepts are positive because they enter a variance."
msgstr ""
"在 GARCH 家族中，`garch_model::egarch` 在**对数**方差上递推，因此负的 `omega` 在那里是允许的；GARCH 与 "
"GJR 的 `omega` 截距为正，因为它们进入方差。"

#: ../../site/guides/portfolio-risk.md:74
msgid "Backtesting what you estimated"
msgstr "回测你估计的东西"

#: ../../site/guides/portfolio-risk.md:76
msgid ""
"`backtest_var` pairs a forecast series with realised returns and reports "
"Kupiec unconditional coverage and Christoffersen independence. "
"`expected_exceptions` is `observations * (1 - confidence_level)`."
msgstr ""
"`backtest_var` 把预测序列与实际收益配对，报告 Kupiec 无条件覆盖与 Christoffersen "
"独立性。`expected_exceptions` 为 `observations * (1 - confidence_level)`。"

